;; Mega Man's mini game, Station Escape: laid out as Mega Man 2's stages go, in screens (16 x 15
;; tiles) the camera moves between one at a time. stage.ts loads it with ?raw, so it is not in the
;; level library, the dev level select or the campaign.
;;
;; The route: a run of five screens along the bottom (the weapon capsule halfway), then a shaft:
;; the ladder at column 71 climbs two screens to a ledge, the ladder at 75 on up through the floor
;; of the top run (three more screens), whose hole at 119-121 drops two screens down a chute into
;; the landing room; then Mega Man 2's two boss shutters (columns 128 and 143, rows 41-42): a
;; one-screen corridor and Dark Mega Man's room (143-158).
;;
;; `screen x y w=N` lines are the camera's sections (each 15 rows high, N columns wide, from
;; column x, row y): it scrolls sideways inside one, and when Mega Man climbs off the top or falls
;; off the bottom it flips a whole screen up or down to the next (scene.ts). The robots of a
;; section are spawned fresh each time Mega Man enters it, as Mega Man 2's are. Past the first
;; shutter the gates lock the camera (the corridor, then the room).
;;
;; Ladders are tiles: L (the ladder, `chain`, drawn as a ladder in the station theme) and E (a
;; ladder's top in a floor, `cloud-ledge`: stood on from above, climbed through from below).
;; The robots and the capsule are the mini game's own entity types (World's `extraEntities`);
;; `screen`, `shutter` and `dark-megaman` are taken out of the map and handled by the scene. The
;; shutters' doorways are solid until they open.
id: mm-station
name: STATION ESCAPE
world: 3
stage: 1
theme: station
music: mm-station
time: 400
start: 2,42
startMode: stand
camera: free
height: 45

[legend]
L chain
E cloud-ledge

